9341	{"artifactId":"LLD-0e1265ed8581e188-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-0e1265ed8581e188-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-16T06:29:09.413Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The derived criteria ac1–ac5 (start a stopped, installed daemon; skip running, errored or not-installed daemons; a failed start shows errored; a plain start; dependants wait for settle) are each designed in a contract, and the non-goals (no install, no update, no setting, no prompt) are not built.","evidence":"activation.ts:77-96 startDaemonIfStopped guards `probed !== 'stopped'`, `isInstalled()`, re-checks `client.reachability()`, then calls `controller.run('start', { plain: true })`. No install call, and no new setting or manifest entry. onSettled (ac5) is designed in §2.1/§2.5 and §3, but is not in the code yet; it is the remaining design delta. [files: vscode-plugin/src/activation.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the update check skips silently when the daemon is unreachable and still marks the plugin version as seen, so before this change a stopped daemon at a plugin upgrade lost the auto-update.","evidence":"daemon-freshness.ts:139 `if (!reachable) return; // skip silently (setLastSeen still runs in finally)` and :187 `await versionState.setLastSeen(versionState.current)` in the finally; :166 selfUpdate = current !== getLastSeen() → performUpdate without a prompt. [files: vscode-plugin/src/freshness/daemon-freshness.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The settings pull, the update check and onboarding all fire at once in extension.ts, in parallel with the activation probe.","evidence":"extension.ts:165 `activateExtension({ client, status, controller })` is followed at once by :175 `void runDaemonFreshnessCheck({`, :242 `void configSync.pullFromDaemon();` and :829-835 the onboarding IIFE. None of them waits for the probe. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"daemon-ctl.sh start stops a live pid-file daemon before spawning, and a start that does not become ready within 60 s exits 4.","evidence":"daemon-ctl.sh:260-264: if the PID_FILE pid is alive it runs `signal_stop` and `wait_for_daemon_stop || force_stop_daemon`. :268-269: `die \"daemon did not become ready within 60 s ...\" 4`. controller.ts:50 maps 4 to 'the daemon git / npm / build / start step failed'. [files: scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A probe reports 'stopped' only when the socket is absent or refuses the connection, and reports 'errored' otherwise, so starting only on 'stopped' is safe.","evidence":"ipc-client.ts:25 `DaemonReachability = 'running' | 'stopped' | 'errored'`. :77-78 ENOENT/ECONNREFUSED give the 'daemon is not running' prefix, which the reachability classification keys off for 'stopped'. activation.ts:45 makes a timeout 'errored'. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts, vscode-plugin/src/activation.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused controller exposes isInstalled() (a check for the built entry) and run(action), and the plain option adds exactly --skip-sync/--skip-install/--skip-build, which daemon-ctl.sh accepts.","evidence":"controller.ts:80-86 isInstalled = existsSync(paths.daemonEntry). :23 PLAIN_FLAGS = ['--skip-sync','--skip-install','--skip-build']. :103 appends them only when options?.plain === true. daemon-ctl.sh:318-320 parses all three, and :255-257 skips sync, install and build accordingly. [files: vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Without options, run builds the same command line as before, so the only other caller (the insrc.daemon.* commands) is unchanged.","evidence":"The only callers of controller.run( are commands.ts:67 `controller.run(action)` and activation.ts:87. controller.ts:103 spreads [] when plain is not true, giving `['bash', ctlScript, action]` as before. [files: vscode-plugin/src/daemon/commands.ts, vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The source-scan tests that pin extension.ts call shapes still pass with the onSettled wiring as described (the onboarding IIFE keeps its guarded form, pullFromDaemon() is still a call, and the freshness block pattern is updated).","evidence":"onboarding/hosts/workspace activation tests match `/void \\(async \\(\\) =>[\\s\\S]*runOnboarding[\\s\\S]*catch \\{/` and `runOnboarding\\(\\{ controller, registrar, ... \\}\\)`; a leading `await` of the settled signal inside the IIFE keeps both. seam.test.ts:47 and truthful-sync.test.ts:209 need `configSync.pullFromDaemon()`, which is kept. extension-wiring.test.ts:27/57/67 need `void runDaemonFreshnessCheck({` and a `\\n  \\}\\);` block terminator; the design names this test as a call site whose block pattern is updated. :27 still passes if the inner call keeps `void`, and :28 forbids `await runDaemonFreshnessCheck`, so the wrapper must not await it directly. [files: vscode-plugin/src/freshness/__tests__/extension-wiring.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/onboarding/__tests__/activation.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/seam.test.ts]","action":"When wrapping, keep `void runDaemonFreshnessCheck({` and avoid `await runDaemonFreshnessCheck`, or update test :28 as well as the block regex.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Nothing stored changes shape. The only persisted state touched is the last-seen plugin version, and the design states its behaviour change: after a plugin upgrade, an auto-started daemon is now self-updated.","evidence":"There is no new globalState or workspaceState key. LAST_SEEN_PLUGIN_VERSION_KEY (extension.ts:85) is read and written by the unchanged freshness module (daemon-freshness.ts:166,187). The LLD edge-case table records the accepted change. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/freshness/daemon-freshness.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each failure ends as a status state and never rejects into activation: a non-zero exit, ok:true while still unreachable, a throwing controller, and a probe timeout. onSettled runs in a finally and is wrapped.","evidence":"activation.ts:88-89 treats ok && state !== 'running' as errored with NO_ANSWER_AFTER_START. :91 shows ok:false as {state:'errored', detail: message}. :93-94 a catch sets errored. :108-112 the chain ends in a .catch. :79 skips 'errored' and 'unknown'. onboarding.ts:62 still offers install when isInstalled is false. Wrapping onSettled in a finally with containment is designed but not yet coded, so it is checked against the design. [files: vscode-plugin/src/activation.ts, vscode-plugin/src/onboarding/onboarding.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1–ac5 maps to at least one named test, and the subjects cover the re-check race, a success while still unreachable, the plain flags and the onSettled ordering.","evidence":"In §5 the acceptance table maps ac1 to 5 tests, ac2 to 2, ac3 to 2, ac4 to 1 and ac5 to 2. The fixture for the re-check asks for a fake client whose answers differ between the probe and the re-check, which matches the two reachability() calls in activation.ts:54 and :83. ac1's live test needs a real VS Code restart and has to be reported rather than run by the gate. [files: vscode-plugin/src/activation.ts]","action":"Report the live ac1 test via `reported` at validate.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-16T06:29:09.413Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
